\
  Key Points:\
\
   * Purpose: Provides a comprehensive interface for administrators to define galaxy structure, team compositions, AI\
     settings, and global game parameters.\
   * Functionality: Allows selection of templates, dynamic generation of configurations, and detailed customization of\
     individual galaxies (name, team count, players per team, AI teams, colony types, distribution mode). Includes global\
     settings for cross-galaxy trading, events, and competition mode. Displays validation issues and statistics.\
\
  Observations:\
\
   * Type Inconsistency: Uses GalaxyFormData internally, which is a simplified version of the Galaxy type, requiring\
     careful mapping. any type assertions are used for gameMode and teamStructureMode.\
   * Functional Bug: Hardcoded `victoryConditions`. The victoryConditions are hardcoded to 'survival', overriding template\
     settings and preventing user selection of other conditions.\
   * Major Inconsistency: Missing `AIConfiguration` integration. The form has its own AI team settings, duplicating and\
     potentially conflicting with the dedicated AIConfiguration.tsx component.\
   * Placeholder: The "Advanced Options" section is a placeholder.\
